00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:07.689
--

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:10.829
I’m sure many of you have wondered why there
are countries with such strange shapes?

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:14.899
For example, have you noticed how weird the
outline of CROATIA is?

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:17.780
Why does it have that kind of fang coming
down?

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.740
It may sound silly, but that fang makes Bosnia
and Herzegovina land-locked.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.340
So what about Russia?

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.109
Why do they have this kind of island between
Lithuania and Poland?

00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:31.209
I mean, who ever decided that this region,
which, by the way, is called KALININGRAD,

00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:32.209
is Russia?

00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:36.020
But, the two that really take the prize, without
a doubt, the countries with the strangest

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.899
shapes are ARMENIA and AZERBAIJAN.

00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:43.689
If you look closely, you will see that Azerbaijan
has a strip of land on the east side of Armenia.

00:01:43.689 --> 00:01:49.020
But within Azerbaijan itself there is another
region that is, in fact, controlled by Armenia.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.990
As you can imagine, all of this is more than
lines on a map.

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:55.739
We are talking about one of the most complex
conflicts in world politics.

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:58.389
A conflict that may be about to be resolved.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:02.059
This video has been made possible by the Munich
Security Conference, but not only because

00:02:02.059 --> 00:02:03.479
they collaborated with us.

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:06.189
It's also that they're an important part of
this whole story.

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:09.810
At the end of the video you will have a much
better understanding about how these borders

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.740
get drawn.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:19.200
Let's go with our story!

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.700
(INTRO)

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.379
Armenia and Azerbaijan are two of those countries
that you will only hear mentioned in the Eurovision

00:02:25.379 --> 00:02:28.360
song competition and... here, on VISUALPOLITIK.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.159
These two countries are neighbours and have
a lot in common.

00:02:31.159 --> 00:02:32.569
Both were Soviet republics.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:41.879
Both countries are extremely corrupt.

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:46.930
Azerbaijan is the private confine of the Aliyev
family, and Armenia has been run for decades

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.769
by an elite group of oligarchs.

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:52.799
As if that were not enough, in both countries
they speak unpronounceable languages.

00:02:52.799 --> 00:02:57.159
To give you an idea, Armenians have their
own unique type of calligraphy, distinct from

00:02:57.159 --> 00:02:58.569
other languages in the world.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:02.470
But with so many similarities between the
two countries, many will think, Well, I'm

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.530
sure they'll get along!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.530
Really?

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.530
Well, no, nothing like that.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.359
Armenia and Azerbaijan hate each other.

00:03:07.359 --> 00:03:08.569
But really hate each other.

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:12.349
The conflict between these two countries has
cost thousands of lives over the past three

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:15.280
decades and caused millions of people to be
displaced.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.190
Come on, this is nothing in comparison to
the Israelis and the Palestinians.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.190
And you'll say...

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.190
Yeah, right Simon!

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.190
Why have we never heard of this conflict?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.609
Well, basically, because there are no left
or right-wings here.

00:03:23.609 --> 00:03:28.230
Instead, Russia has always been supporting
the Armenians and Turkey, the Azerbaijanis.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.549
The United States has no interest in this
story.

00:03:30.549 --> 00:03:34.370
And since there are no good guys here, the
victims don’t get much attention.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.859
At this point, many of you will be wondering
why it is they hate each other so much.

00:03:38.859 --> 00:03:40.569
Is it a matter of ideologies?

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:42.219
Is it because of natural resources?

00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:43.609
Well, neither of those.

00:03:43.609 --> 00:03:48.549
It is true that Armenians are Christians and
Azerbaijanis, also called AZERI, are Muslims.

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:50.930
But religion is not the reason.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.290
The subject of discord is this piece of land
you see here.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.349
(MAP NAGORNO KARABAKH)

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:04.749
This region here is called NAGORNO-KARABAKH,
and it has about 140,000 inhabitants of which

00:04:04.749 --> 00:04:06.599
90% speak Armenian.

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:08.290
Armenia says that it belongs to them.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.239
But officially, it belongs to Azerbaijan.

00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:11.389
So what's in that region?

00:04:11.389 --> 00:04:12.409
Does it have oil?

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:13.409
No.

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:14.909
Is it of any strategic importance?

00:04:14.909 --> 00:04:15.909
Minimal!

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:24.680
So why are we telling you this story here,
on VisualPolitik?

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.650
Well for three reasons: the first is because
this conflict may be resolved very soon.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:33.410
The second is because we have had the privilege
of watching one of the episodes of this story

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.410
play out live.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.410
And yes, I say that because this has happened
before my very own eyes.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:37.919
As you know, VisualPolitik is one of the media
outlets that was invited to go to the Munich

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:39.060
Security Conference.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.773
And right at the hotel where this conference
was held was one of those peace talks.

00:04:41.773 --> 00:04:42.773
I mean, a lot of the things I'm going to tell
you, our team have seen with their own eyes.

00:04:42.773 --> 00:04:43.773
You've got to understand that it’s not every
day you see history happening live.

00:04:43.773 --> 00:04:44.773
So I had my reasons for making this video
but there's a third reason as well!

00:04:44.773 --> 00:04:46.259
This is one of those stories that proves how
absurd politics can very often be.

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:50.000
Because yes, here we’re talking about two
countries killing themselves for a piece of

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.490
land that is worth absolutely NOTHING.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.900
It has no oil, no strategic value...

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:55.900
Nothing.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.220
I think looking at this issue might help many
of us to realize how absurd many debates are

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:03.639
in which sides just become rigid in defending
a particular stance.

00:05:03.639 --> 00:05:04.639
But listen.

00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:06.760
What is going on between Armenia in Azerbaijan?

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.690
Why do they hate each other so much?

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.490
Does the conflict have a solution?

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.921
Today we're going to answer these questions
but first, let's look at some history.

00:05:13.921 --> 00:05:21.240
(TITLE: THE 
PEACE NO ONE WANTED)

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:24.600
The really big question is... who was in Nagorno-Karabakh
first?

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.870
The Armenians or the Azerbaijanis?

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.900
And you can probably guess the answer: it
depends who you ask.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:34.190
What we do know is that throughout the 1920s,
the majority of the population was Armenian.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:38.370
This is when Stalin arrived and conquered
the entire region and then divided it into

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:42.330
three socialist republics: Georgia, Armenia
and Azerbaijan.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.310
And what did Stalin's division do?

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:49.400
Well, just what he’d wished.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:55.690
So in 1923, Stalin said "This Nagorno-Karabakh
thing is going to be part of Azerbaijan, Why?

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:59.169
Because I say so, I am Stalin and I’m here,
and the rest of the world can just shut up."

00:05:59.169 --> 00:06:02.099
The Soviet Union never really looked when
it came to drawing borders.

00:06:02.099 --> 00:06:05.979
And no ethnic group or nationalist movement
dared to question Moscow's decisions.

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:14.919
So, until 1987, no-one dared to say they wanted
to be part of Armenia, and what happened in

00:06:14.919 --> 00:06:15.919
1987?

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:18.139
Well, the Soviet Union was starting to disintegrate.

00:06:18.139 --> 00:06:22.889
And all of a sudden, a whole lot of Armenians
organized a referendum on self-determination

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:27.020
to get out of Azerbaijan and, if possible,
to be part of Armenia.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:31.040
As you can imagine, this sparked a famous
war between Armenia and Azerbaijan, which

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:37.110
lasted until 1994.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:43.130
Six years of war that took the lives of more
than 30,000 and left more than a million people

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.770
displaced.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.210
So who won the war?

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.610
Well, in practice, we can say that Armenia
did.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.349
Officially, Nagorno-Karabakh is part of Azerbaijan.

00:06:52.349 --> 00:06:56.860
But the reality is that the region is ruled
by the Republic of ARTSAKH, where the language,

00:06:56.860 --> 00:07:04.150
the currency and even the banks are the same
as in Armenia.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:08.310
As if this were not enough, all the borders
of this area are controlled by the Armenian

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:09.310
army.

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:14.080
Come on, although almost no country recognizes
Artsakh as an Armenian region, in practice

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.080
it is one.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.169
And you're probably thinking, but what about
the Azerbaijanis who live there?

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:21.189
Well, the truth is, almost everyone had to
leave after the war.

00:07:21.189 --> 00:07:25.229
If we count up those who live in this region
and those who lived in Armenia, we’re talking

00:07:25.229 --> 00:07:27.360
about a total of 800,000 Azerbaijanis.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:32.449
And it was a similar story with the Armenians
who lived in Azerbaijan.

00:07:32.449 --> 00:07:35.439
Conclusion: to this day, both peoples hate
each other.

00:07:35.439 --> 00:07:36.909
And I’m not exaggerating.

00:07:36.909 --> 00:07:38.110
Here’s an example.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:42.730
In 2005, the then Mayor of Baku, the capital
of Azerbaijan, had an official meeting with

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.000
a German delegation.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:48.410
Watch out for this gem of diplomacy, you can’t
miss it.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:53.560
(AUDIO: Our goal is the complete elimination
of Armenians.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:58.330
You, Nazis, already eliminated the Jews in
the 1930s and 40s, right?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.710
You should be able to understand us.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:04.219
–Hajibala Abutalybov, Mayor of Baku in 2005)

00:08:04.219 --> 00:08:06.930
Okay, some of you will be thinking...

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:10.030
"Ok, but that guy was just a mayor..."

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:14.819
Well, take a look at the current president
of Azerbaijan, Ilham Aliyev.

00:08:14.819 --> 00:08:21.550
(AUDIO: ...Our main enemies are Armenians
of the world and the hypocritical and corrupt

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.509
politicians under their control.

00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:26.160
–Ilham Aliyev, Azerbaijan president)

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.569
If you're a regular VisualPolitik follower,
Aliyev's name is familiar.

00:08:29.569 --> 00:08:32.760
You know we're talking about a corrupt dictator
with few rivals.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:37.450
And as you know, corrupt dictators love to
point out an enemy: The Yanks, the Jews, or,

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.390
in this case, the Armenians.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:44.080
And that helps to explain why every time someone
has sat down to negotiate a peace agreement,

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.080
they have failed.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.530
Let's be honest, neither side wants peace!

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:51.150
And you're probably thinking surely there
must be some possible agreement?

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.150
Of course!

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:56.750
In 2009, the Organization for Security and
Cooperation in Europe sat Aliyev and the then

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.880
President of Armenia down at the same table.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:00.890
And where did they do it?

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:01.890
In Madrid.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:06.770
That's where they set out a series of principles.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:12.980
Basically, the inhabitants of Nagorno-Karabakh,
or if you prefer, the REPUBLIC OF ARTSAKH

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.850
could decide whether they wanted their land
to be part of Armenia or Azerbaijan.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:20.870
The Armenian army would have to withdraw from
the surrounding areas and Azerbaijan would

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:24.140
guarantee a corridor between this region and
Armenia.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:25.360
Makes sense, doesn't it?

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.170
Well, yes, on paper it does make real sense.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.910
But unfortunately, neither side was willing
to accept it.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:35.160
At the end of the day, having an arch rival
has been a great blessing to the oligarchs

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.160
of both countries.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.580
However, now things could be set to change.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:39.580
Why?

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:43.600
Well, we're going to look into that right
now.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:48.810
(HEADLINE: THE ARMENIAN OUTSIDER)

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:52.100
Armenia is one of the few countries in the
world that has more citizens outside of its

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:53.100
borders than inside.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.310
As it stands today, some three million people
live within Armenia.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.810
But the Armenian diaspora totals more than
10 million people.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:02.440
So why are so many people leaving Armenia?

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:07.500
Well, at home they have more than 20% unemployment,
they have the same per capita income as Namibia

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.900
and corruption is around every corner.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:15.080
And once again, the conflict in Nagorno-Karabakh
is the perfect scapegoat for all its problems.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.150
What’s more, almost all the political elite
come from this country.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:22.340
In fact, the former Armenian Prime Minister
was born in the Republic of Artsakh, the former

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:26.000
Prime Minister of Armenia was also born in
the Republic of Artsakh and the same goes

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.060
for lots of senior officials.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:33.320
And believe me, strange as it may seem, the
blissful Republic of Artsach is the number

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:47.700
one priority of all the governments this country
has had.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.980
Armenia might have all the corruption you
can imagine, but its presidents did such useful

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:57.210
things as trying to convince the government
of TUVALU to recognize Artsach as an independent

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.210
republic.

00:10:58.210 --> 00:11:01.450
Yes, that’s right, TUVALU, one of those
tiny, forgotten countries in the Pacific.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:02.820
And the list goes on.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:07.160
Today there are six states in the United States
that recognize the Republic of Artsakh.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.420
And you'll say, individual states within the
United States?

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:13.830
What business does California have in recognizing
sovereign states?

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:14.830
Well, nothing.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:19.590
But that's how lots of Armenian politicians
have been justifying their pay check for years...

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:22.890
Until we get to 2018.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:30.080
(AUDIO: Armenian protesters brought down a
prime minister - Washington Post)

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.080
https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/monkey-cage/wp/2018/04/30/armenian-protesters-brought-down-a-prime-minister-heres-why-theyre-in-the-streets/

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.080
Exactly!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.570
We covered this here on VisualPolitik, in
2018 the Armenians had had enough after so

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:39.640
many years of corruption, abuse of power and
the poverty that is a consequence of such

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.260
a situation and drove their Prime Minister
out.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:45.950
The new Armenian government is led by the
man you see on screen, Nikol Pashinyan.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:50.370
In his first two years of rule he has carried
out several economic reforms and appears to

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.440
be fighting corruption seriously.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:56.160
And you're going to say, so what does this
man think of the conflict?

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:01.280
Well... this probably won’t surprise you...

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:06.130
(AUDIO: Pashinyan calls for unification between
Armenia and Karabakh - Eurasianet)

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.130
https://eurasianet.org/pashinyan-calls-for-unification-between-armenia-and-karabakh

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:10.650
And I know what you're probably thinking:
that’s hardly original these days, right?

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:13.010
Well, yes, and no at the same time.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:17.230
First, Pashinyan is the first Prime Minister
in years not to be born in that region.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:21.250
Second, he is an absolute outsider when it
comes to the Armenian elites.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:25.800
In other words, he doesn’t need to fuel
the fear of Azerbaijan to gain popularity.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.180
And that's why it's an opportune moment to
negotiate a peace agreement.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:32.710
The question is... how exactly are peace agreements
negotiated?

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:37.230
Let’s take a look.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:41.350
(TITLE: THE MUNICH SECURITY CONFERENCE)

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:45.010
Imagine for a moment that you have been hired
as advisers to the Armenian government and

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.780
you want to negotiate with Azerbaijan, where
would you start?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.340
Maybe you'd try to get the number to Baku's
presidential palace.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:52.890
Let’s say you call "hey, is Aliyev here?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.540
Look, I’m calling from the Government of
Armenia about Nagorno..."

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.580
Chances are they'll hang up the phone.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.920
That's what political conferences are for.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.040
That's where
political leaders from all over the world

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.730
come together, and they can talk one-to-one,
face-to-face.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:08.400
Well, the Munich Security Conference is one
of the largest.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:18.000
(“Part of our mission is to offer a relatively
easy platform for people who normally find

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:27.850
it very hard to visit each other’s country
because that is often seen as a difficult

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.240
step.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:35.180
You lose face by going to visit your adversary
so they come to Munich and they meet here.”

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.180
Wolfgang Ischinger)

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.180
(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IP3rD1iz8d0&amp;t=680s
1.53)

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:39.830
The gentleman you just saw is Wolfgang Ischinger,
the director of the Munich Security Conference.

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:44.180
Basically, that gentleman and his team have
a list of the names and numbers of all the

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.300
politicians who are going to attend the conference.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:50.510
So, in this case, we could talk to him and
say "Look, Wolfgang, we want to contact those

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:55.130
guys from Azerbaijan, with whom you already
know we have ongoing issues..." or, even more

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:59.200
likely: he would have approached us himself,
"Guys, why don't you get together?"

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:06.880
(AUDIO: “The president of Azerbaijan and
the Prime Minister of Armenia... they have

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:13.670
a conflict called Nagorno-Karabakh which has
been going on for practically 30 years now

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.350
where people are being killed all the time.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:19.440
Not in huge numbers but people die.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:26.322
So yesterday we organized a session for these
two and both of them told me: this is actually

00:14:26.322 --> 00:14:29.590
the first time we show up together anywhere”
Wolfgang Ischinger

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.590
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IP3rD1iz8d0&amp;t=680s
Min 2.19)

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.590
You heard what the man said.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:35.870
And we can tell you this because one of our
team was there and saw it with his own eyes.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:39.200
Pashynian and Aliyev were arguing together
on the same stage.

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.630
And then you'll say come on, Simon!

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.040
Are you telling me that two leaders who hate
each other went to some German conference

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:48.110
hand in hand and then sang “Kumbaya” for
a photo opportunity and now everything is

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.110
sorted?

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.110
Not really.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:53.120
In fact, throughout the debate they devoted
themselves to discussing historical data to

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:57.410
justify why Nagorno-Karabakh should belong
to one side or the other.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.230
It wasn't a friendly chat.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:03.800
But the truth is that in this type of conference,
the least important things are the on-stage

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:04.800
debates.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.410
The real action is what happens in the cafes,
and in the hotels.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.410
Sometimes even in the hotel rooms!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.310
For that reason, at the Munich Security Conference,
the rooms are prepared so that the various

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:13.430
delegations can sit down and negotiate.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.800
The next time you hear about two countries
that have signed an agreement, think that

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:25.920
most likely, that agreement was previously
discussed on the sofa of a hotel suite.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:31.860
And, as far as the conference was concerned,
both the Azerbaijani and Armenian delegations

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:35.550
had more than one chance to have coffee together
and talk about their situation.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:37.800
Does this mean they've already signed a peace
agreement?

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.800
Not really.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.700
But it means it looks like an agreement could
be reached.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.420
But in this case I can't show you any data
yet.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.650
Just our personal hunch.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:48.850
And yes, I know, here at VisualPolitik we
like to base everything we say on supporting

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.780
facts and statistics, not just on a few rumours
we've heard.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.210
But, in this case, there's still not much
hard evidence.

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:58.330
In the meantime, I leave you with this question:
Do you think that Armenia and Azerbaijan will

00:15:58.330 --> 00:15:59.420
end up reaching a peace agreement?

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.190
What would be the consequences of this for
these two countries?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.680
You can leave me your answer in the comments.

